0.45,\n        0.78,\n        0.12\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n        \"source\": \"fastapi_documentation.pdf\",\n        \"page\": 12,\n        \"category\": \"programming\",\n        \"author\": \"OpenAI\"\n    }\n}\n```\n\nLet's understand each field.\n\n| Field     | Purpose                              |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| ID        | Uniquely identifies a record         |\n| Text      | Original content                     |\n| Embedding | Numerical representation             |\n| Metadata  | Additional information for filtering |\n\n**Why store metadata?**\n\nImagine a user asks:\n\n> Explain FastAPI authentication from the official documentation.\n\nYou can search semantically while filtering:\n\n```py\nfilter = {    \n    \"category\": \"programming\",\n    \"source\": \"fastapi_documentation.pdf\"\n}\n```\n\nThis allows you to combine semantic search with traditional filtering.\n\n## How data looks in a database\n\n| id | sentence | embedding | metadata |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | I love machine learning | `[0.21, 0.45, 0.78, ...]` | `{\"category\": \"AI\", \"source\": \"doc1.pdf\"}` |\n| 2 | Python is a programming language | `[0.32, 0.12, 0.89, ...]` | `{\"category\": \"programming\", \"source\": \"doc2.pdf\"}` |\n| 3 | Artificial intelligence is fascinating | `[0.56, 0.23, 0.67, ...]` | `{\"category\": \"AI\", \"source\": \"doc3.pdf\"}` |\n\nThe embedding column stores the entire vector (for example, 384 floating-point values), not just the first and last five values.\n\n## Embeddings using SQLite\n\n### Store Embeddings\n\nSQLite is a simple database that you can use to understand how embedding storage works.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\nimport sqlite3\nimport json\n\n# Connect to database\nconn = sqlite3.connect(\"embeddings.db\")\ncursor = conn.cursor()\n\n# Create table\ncursor.execute(\"\"\"\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sentences (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    sentence TEXT,\n    embedding TEXT,\n    metadata TEXT\n)\n\"\"\")\n\n# Generate and store embeddings\nfor i, sentence in enumerate(sentences1):\n\n    embedding = model.encode(sentence2)\n\n    # Create metadata\n    metadata = {\n        \"category\": \"AI\",\n        \"source\": \"document.pdf\",\n        \"page\": i + 1\n    }\n\n    cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n        INSERT INTO sentences (sentence, embedding, metadata)\n        VALUES (?, ?, ?)\n    \"\"\", (\n        sentence,\n        json.dumps(embedding.tolist()),\n        json.dumps(metadata)\n    ))\n    print(\"All sentences successfully stored in SQLite!\")\n\nconn.commit()\nconn.close()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-02T16:24:08.149328Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-02T16:24:08.14978Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-02T16:24:08.233498Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-02T16:24:08.149745Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-02T16:24:08.232512Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"All sentences successfully stored in SQLite!\nAll sentences successfully stored in SQLite!\nAll sentences successfully stored in SQLite!\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":13},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Here:\n\n- `sentence` stores the original text.\n- `embedding` stores the vector as a JSON string.\n- `embedding.tolist()` converts the NumPy array into a Python list.\n- `json.dumps()` converts that list into a string for SQLite storage.\n\n### Retrieve Embeddings\n\nNow let's retrieve the stored vectors.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Connect to database\nconn = sqlite3.connect(\"embeddings.db\")\ncursor = conn.cursor()\n\ncursor.execute(\"SELECT id, sentence, embedding, metadata FROM sentences\")\n\nprint(f\"{'ID':<5} | {'Sentence':<35} | {'Embedding':<45} | {'Metadata'}\")\nprint(\"-\" * 120)\n\nfor row in cursor.fetchall():\n\n    embedding = json.loads(row[2])\n    metadata = json.loads(row[3])\n\n    embedding_display = f\"{embedding[:5]} ... {embedding[-5