ext":"I love machine learning Score: 0.816496580927726\nI like eating pizza Score: 0.0\nI enjoy coding Score: 0.0\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":25},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"You might wonder: If TF IDF already calculates word importance, why do we need cosine similarity?\n\nBecause they perform two different jobs:\n\n| TF IDF | Cosine Similarity |\n| --- | --- |\n| Calculates word importance | Measures vector similarity |\n| Converts text into vectors | Compares vectors |\n| Generates numerical representations | Generates similarity scores |\n\n## BM25 (Best Matching 25)\n\nBM25 is a ranking algorithm widely used in modern search engines and hybrid retrieval systems.\n\nIt improves upon traditional TF IDF by considering:\n\n1. Term frequency.\n2. Inverse document frequency.\n3. Document length normalization.\n4. Term frequency saturation.\n\nThe BM25 formula is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nBM25(D,Q)=\\sum_{t\\in Q}&IDF(t)\\\\\n&\\times\n\\frac{f(t,D)(k_1+1)}\n{f(t,D)+k_1(1-b+b\\frac{|D|}{avgdl})}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhere:\n\n| Parameter | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| $D$ | Document |\n| $Q$ | Search query |\n| $f(t,D)$ | Frequency of term in document |\n| $IDF(t)$ | Inverse document frequency |\n| $\\|D\\|$ | Document length |\n| $avgdl$ | Average document length |\n| $k_1$ | Controls term frequency saturation |\n| $b$ | Controls document length normalization |\n\nTypical values are:\n\n- $k_1 = 1.2$ to $2.0$\n- $b = 0.75$\n\n### Why BM25 is better than basic TF IDF\n\nImagine two documents:\n\n- D1: `Vector database` (2 words)\n- D2: `Vector database` repeated 50 times in a long document.\n\nA basic term frequency approach might give D2 an excessively high score because the query terms appear many times.\n\nBM25 uses term frequency saturation, meaning that repeating a term 50 times does not necessarily make the document 50 times more relevant.\n\nIt also normalizes for document length, helping avoid unfairly favoring longer documents.\n\nIn vector databases: BM25 is particularly useful for retrieving documents that contain exact keywords, technical terms, product names, identifiers, or specific phrases.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"pip install rank-bm25","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-02T16:24:32.925917Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-02T16:24:32.926265Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-02T16:24:35.594205Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-02T16:24:32.926224Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-02T16:24:35.592953Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Collecting rank-bm25\n  Downloading rank_bm25-0.2.2-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (3.2 kB)\nRequirement already satisfied: numpy in /usr/local/lib/python3.13/dist-packages (from rank-bm25) (2.1.3)\nDownloading rank_bm25-0.2.2-py3-none-any.whl (8.6 kB)\nInstalling collected packages: rank-bm25\nSuccessfully installed rank-bm25-0.2.2\nNote: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":26},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from rank_bm25 import BM25Okapi\n\nquery = \"Machine Learning\"\n\n# Step 1: Tokenize documents\ntokenized_documents = [\n    doc.lower().split()\n    for doc in sentences1\n]\ntokenized_documents","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-02T16:24:35.595583Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-02T16:24:35.595939Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-02T16:24:35.609246Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-02T16:24:35.595902Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-02T16:24:35.608077Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":27,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"[['i', 'love', 'machine', 'learning'],\n ['i', 'enjoy', 'coding'],\n ['i', 'like', 'eating', 'pizza']]"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":27},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Step 2: Initialize BM25\nbm25 = BM25Okapi(tokenized_documents)\nbm25","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-02T16:24:35.615818Z","iopub.execute_input"